---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getCatalogue } from '../lib/catalogue';

const { stats } = await getCatalogue();
---

<Layout title="About" description="What the ID Tracker is, where its information comes from and what it deliberately leaves out.">
  <div class="wrap pt-10">
    <p class="eyebrow mb-3">About</p>
    <h1 class="display max-w-3xl text-4xl uppercase sm:text-5xl">A reference, not a download page</h1>

    <div class="mt-10 grid max-w-3xl gap-10 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-fg/85">
      <section>
        <h2 class="display-sm mb-3 text-xl text-fg">What this is</h2>
        <p>
          Martin Garrix has played, teased and shelved far more music than he has released. Fans have kept track of it
          for years in spreadsheets. This site puts that record in one place: {stats.tracks} songs and {stats.entries} known
          versions from {stats.firstYear} to {stats.lastYear}, with who was involved, where each was first played, and how
          much of it has ever been heard.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="display-sm mb-3 text-xl text-fg">What it leaves out</h2>
        <p>
          No audio is hosted here and nothing on this site links to a leaked file. Where a version is marked as
          circulating, that is a statement about the historical record, not a pointer to it. The links you will find are
          citations: live-set videos, tracklists, interviews and posts by the artists themselves.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="display-sm mb-3 text-xl text-fg">Where the information comes from</h2>
        <p>
          The catalogue was compiled from two community-maintained trackers and then merged by hand: the same recording
          often appeared in both under different names, years or credits. Where the two disagreed, one reading was chosen
          and the other kept on file. Notes are the community's own and have been lightly edited.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          A few entries are marked as officially released. That means a later version of the song came out; the entry
          documents the demo, early vocal or live version that did not.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="display-sm mb-3 text-xl text-fg">Corrections</h2>
        <p>
          This is a fan project and it will contain mistakes: a wrong year, a misattributed vocalist, two versions that
          are really one. If you spot something, tell the PlusXHub team and it will be fixed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="display-sm mb-3 text-xl text-fg">Affiliation</h2>
        <p>
          The ID Tracker is run by fans. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or connected to Martin Garrix, STMPD
          RCRDS, Spinnin' Records or any other artist or label named here. All song titles and artist names belong to
          their owners.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
